From: Nahum Shalman <nshalman@edgecast.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Jun 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Populate PeerInfo on illumos via getpeerucred

getPeerInfo() in src/nix/unix/daemon.cc has per-platform arms for
SO_PEERCRED (Linux, OpenBSD) and LOCAL_PEERCRED (macOS, FreeBSD).
illumos has neither, so the function returns an empty PeerInfo and
the daemon logs "accepted connection from pid <unknown>, user
<unknown>" for every client. Worse, authPeer() then sees peer.uid ==
nullopt, getpwuid() is not called, the user name resolves to
"<unknown>", and trusted-users / allowed-users matching falls back to
"*"-only — defeating the mandatory-access-control story for
multi-user setups on illumos.

illumos exposes peer credentials through getpeerucred(3C), declared
in <ucred.h>. It populates an opaque ucred_t *, from which
ucred_geteuid / ucred_getegid / ucred_getpid extract the effective
uid, gid, and pid of the peer at connect time. The effective ids are
the right choice: authPeer() uses them to decide trust, matching
macOS's xucred.cr_uid and Linux's struct ucred.uid (both effective
on an AF_UNIX connect).

Add a parallel #elif defined(__sun) arm. The pattern matches the
existing arms: best-effort extraction, leave fields nullopt on
failure (authPeer handles std::nullopt gracefully — it just yields a
"<unknown>" user name and skips trust elevation). The <ucred.h>
include sits next to the existing <sys/ucred.h> block, guarded by
__sun (illumos's <ucred.h> is unrelated to BSD's <sys/ucred.h>:
different header, different API, opaque vs concrete struct).

After this patch, with nix-daemon running as root on illumos and a
non-root client connecting via /nix/var/nix/daemon-socket/socket, the
log reads "accepted connection from pid 12345, user alice" and
trusted-users / @group matching works as expected.

---
 src/nix/unix/daemon.cc | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc
+++ b/src/nix/unix/daemon.cc
@@ -43,6 +43,10 @@
 #  include <sys/ucred.h>
 #endif

+#ifdef __sun
+#  include <ucred.h>
+#endif
+
 using namespace nix;
 using namespace nix::daemon;

@@ -264,6 +268,16 @@
     if (getsockopt(remote, SOL_LOCAL, LOCAL_PEERCRED, &cred, &credLen) == 0)
         peer.uid = cred.cr_uid;

+#elif defined(__sun)
+
+    ucred_t * cred = nullptr;
+    if (getpeerucred(remote, &cred) == 0) {
+        peer.pid = ucred_getpid(cred);
+        peer.uid = ucred_geteuid(cred);
+        peer.gid = ucred_getegid(cred);
+        ucred_free(cred);
+    }
+
 #endif

     return peer;
